[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to improper handling of user authentication data, which can lead to a security risk known as Credential Stuffing. This vulnerability arises when the application allows users to log in using email and password combinations without implementing adequate rate limiting or account lockout mechanisms. If an attacker can repeatedly attempt to log in with various credentials, they may exploit this weakness to gain unauthorized access to user accounts, especially if users reuse passwords across different services. The lack of protective measures against such brute-force attacks can compromise user accounts and sensitive information.

